the crops have withered  the grass has turned to dust  and the animals that support millions  are dying  where seasonal rains brought life to the  borderlands of ethiopia somalia and  kenya  bone dry winds now blow  it hasn't rained here for three years  most people here are pastoralists they  follow their animals and live from the  land  but the shortage of water has driven  many into camps  thousands live here in this ad hoc  settlement in ethiopia  and the aid agencies are struggling to  feed them  the un says 13 million are facing severe  hunger  others still crisscross the territory  searching for water if their livestock  can manage it  but if the animals die malnutrition  typically follows for they are the only  source of meat and milk  unicef says hundreds of thousands of  children are now at risk of severe  malnutrition what will happen in your  view if we don't get  significant rainfall  in april  oh god no this year i mean  it is a possibility  which i would not like even to think of  but i mean professionally i have to  and i think  it can be a real catastrophe a huge  catastrophe  in somalia the drought has been  particularly fierce 90 percent of the  country has been affected and many have  abandoned their homes in search of food  and water  aid agencies say there is still time to  act but the lives of millions are at  risk  john sparks sky news
 

